<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-RESULTS OF FEATURE RACES AT LONGCHAMP.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-RESULTS OF FEATURE RACES AT LONGCHAMP.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of feature races at</p>
<p>Longchamp on Saturday:</p>
<p>Group two Prix de Royallieu for three-year-olds and upwards,</p>
<p>run over one mile four and a half furlongs (2.5 kms)</p>
<p>1. Annaba (ridden by Frankie Dettori)</p>
<p>2. Whitewater Affair (Jason Weaver)</p>
<p>3. Zafzala (Gerald Mosse)</p>
<p>13 ran</p>
<p>Distances: Four lengths, nose</p>
<p>Winner owned by Sheikh Mohammed and trained in England by</p>
<p>John Gosden.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 39,526 sterling (65,000 dollars)</p>
<p>Pari-mutuel (to and including one franc stake)</p>
<p>Win (coupled with Spanish Falls) 10.20; places 5.30, 5.30,</p>
<p>1.50; Forecast 181.20</p>
<p>Group one Prix du Cardan for four-year-olds and upwards, run</p>
<p>over two and a half miles (4 kms):</p>
<p>1. Nononito (Thierry Jarnet)</p>
<p>2. Moonax (Frankie Dettori)</p>
<p>3. Always Earnest (Alain Badel)</p>
<p>10 ran</p>
<p>Distances: One length, 2 1/2.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Patrick Sebagh and trained in France by Jean</p>
<p>Lesbordes</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 65,876 sterling ($103,100)</p>
<p>Pari-mutuel: Win 19.70; places 3.70, 1.90, 3.30; Forecast</p>
<p>29.30.</p>
</text>
